      "source": [
        "# Edith MT5 Demo Runtime\n",
        "\n",
        "This notebook connects to a configured **MetaTrader 5 demo account**, evaluates XAUUSD signals continuously, and submits guarded demo orders.\n",
        "\n",
        "It refuses non-demo accounts, requires explicit confirmation, keeps credentials in environment variables, limits Edith-owned open positions, and publishes heartbeat, signals, order responses, deals, balance, equity, profit, and connection status to the dashboard.\n",
        "\n",
        "Stop the loop with **Kernel → Interrupt**.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "edith-configuration",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Required environment variables\n",
        "\n",
        "Install locally on the same Windows machine as the MT5 terminal:\n",
        "\n",
        "```powershell\n",
        "python -m pip install -e \".[mt5]\"\n",
        "$env:LILITH_EXECUTION_MODE = \"mt5-demo\"\n",
        "$env:EDITH_MT5_CONFIRM_DEMO = \"YES\"\n",
        "$env:MT5_LOGIN = \"YOUR_DEMO_LOGIN\"\n",
        "$env:MT5_PASSWORD = \"YOUR_DEMO_PASSWORD\"\n",
        "$env:MT5_SERVER = \"YOUR_DEMO_SERVER\"\n",
        "$env:EDITH_MT5_SYMBOL = \"XAUUSDm\"\n",
        "$env:EDITH_MT5_TIMEFRAME = \"M5\"\n",
        "$env:EDITH_MT5_LOT = \"0.01\"\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "The MetaTrader 5 desktop terminal must be open, logged in to the same demo account, connected, and algorithmic trading must be enabled.\n"
      ]
    },
